{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 47,
  "title": "The legend of the seven Maruts",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga47/balasans47.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga47/balaitrans47.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "The legend of Seven-Maruts, the Seven-Wind gods, and the legend of the kings of Vishaala are narrated to Rama and Lakshmana, while Vishvamitra is narrating the legend of Vishaala. At the request of Diti, Indra blesses the seven segments of her foetus to become saptamarudgaNa-s, Seven Wind gods, and the place where the legend of Indra-Diti has happened, that province later became the City of Vishaala."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे सप्तचत्वारिंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 47th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.47.1",
      "label": "1.47.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "सप्तधा तु कृते गर्भे दितिः परमदुःखिता |\nसहस्राक्षं दुराधर्षं वाक्यं सानुनयाब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "saptadhā tu kṛte garbhe ditiḥ parama duḥkhitā |\nsahasrākṣam durādharṣam vākyam sa anunayā abravīt",
      "translation": "\"Diti was highly anguished when her foetus is rendered into sevenfold, and spoke these appeasing words to the indomitable Thousand-eyed Indra.\" Thus Vishvamitra continued his narration about City Vishala.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "garbhe saptadhaa tu kR^ite",
          "iast": "garbhe saptadhā tu kṛte",
          "devanagari": "गर्भे सप्तधा तु कृते",
          "meaning": "foetus, into seven ways, but, on rendering",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ditiH parama duHkhitaa",
          "iast": "ditiḥ parama duḥkhitā",
          "devanagari": "दितिः परम दुःखिता",
          "meaning": "Diti, highly, anguished",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "duraadharSam sahasraakSam",
          "iast": "durādharṣam sahasrākṣam",
          "devanagari": "दुराधर्षं सहस्राक्षं",
          "meaning": "to indomitable one, Thousand-eyed Indra",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa anunayaa vaakyam abraviit",
          "iast": "sa anunayā vākyam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "स अनुनया वाक्यं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "with, appeasement, words, spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.47.2",
      "label": "1.47.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "ममापराधाद्गर्भोऽयं सप्तधा शकलीकृतः |\nनापराधो हि देवेश तवात्र बलसूदन",
      "iast": "mama aparādhāt garbho ayam saptadhā śakalī kṛtaḥ |\nna aparādho hi deva īśa tava atra balasūdana",
      "translation": "\" 'Oh, Indra, the eliminator of demon Bala, this foetus of mine is sliced into seven segments owing to my own misdeed, oh, ruler of gods, Indra, indeed there is no iniquity of yours in this matter.' Thus Diti started speaking to Indra.",
