    {
      "id": "1.47.6",
      "label": "1.47.6",
      "numbers": [
        6
      ],
      "devanagari": "चत्वारस्तु सुरश्रेष्ठ दिशो वै तव शासनात् |\nसंचरिष्यन्ति भद्रं ते कलेन हि ममात्मजाः\nत्वत्कृतेनैव नाम्ना वै मारुता इति विश्रुताः |",
      "iast": "catvāraḥ tu suraśreṣṭha diśo vai tava śāsanāt |\nsañcariṣyanti bhadram te kalena hi mama ātmajāḥ\ntvat kṛtena eva nāmnā vai mārutā iti viśrutāḥ |",
      "translation": "\" 'Oh, chief of gods, Indra, let four of my sons permeate four directions according to time and at your command, let safety betide you, and let them be renowned verily by the name given by you as 'Marut,' because you have coaxed the crying fragments of foetus saying, 'maa ruda, maa ruda, 'do not cry, do not cry...' Thus Diti said to Indra.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "sura shreSTha",
          "iast": "sura śreṣṭha",
          "devanagari": "सुर श्रेष्ठ",
          "meaning": "oh, god's, chief",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "catvaaraH mama aatma jaaH",
          "iast": "catvāraḥ mama ātma jāḥ",
