          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.47.7",
      "label": "1.47.7",
      "numbers": [
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "तस्यास्तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा सहस्राक्षः पुरंदरः\nउवाच प्रांजलिर्वाक्यं दितिं बलनिषूदनः |",
      "iast": "tasyāḥ tat vacanam śrutvā sahasrākṣaḥ purandaraḥ\nuvāca prāñjaliḥ vākyam ditim balasūdanaḥ |",
      "translation": "\"On hearing her words, the Thousand-eyed destroyer of enemy's citadels and a demon named Bala, namely Indra, spoke this word to Diti, humbly adjoining his palms.",
