    {
      "id": "1.47.11",
      "label": "1.47.11, 12",
      "numbers": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "devanagari": "इक्ष्वाकोस्तु नरव्याघ्र पुत्रः परमधार्मिकः\nअलंबुषायामुत्पन्नो विशाल इति विश्रुतः |\nतेन चासीदिह स्थाने विशालेति पुरी कृता",
      "iast": "ikṣvākostu naravyāghra putraḥ parama dhārmikaḥ\nalambuṣāyām utpanno viśāla iti viśrutaḥ |\ntena ca āsīt iha sthāne viśāle iti purī kṛtā",
      "translation": "\"To king Ikshvaku of Vishaala, oh, tigerly-man Rama, a highly righteous son was born through queen Alambusa, and he was renowned as Vishaala. There is a city in this place constructed by him and known by his own name, Vishaala.",
      "notes": [
        "These Ikshvaku-s of Vishaala are not the Ikshvaku-s of Ayodhya, i.e., of Solar Dynasty. The Bhaagavata Puraana says separately in its seventh canto about this dynasty of Ikshvaku-s of Vishaala."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "naravyaaghra",
          "iast": "naravyāghra",
          "devanagari": "नरव्याघ्र",
          "meaning": "oh, tigerly-man, Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ikSvaakoH tu",
          "iast": "ikṣvākoḥ tu",
          "devanagari": "इक्ष्वाकोः तु",
          "meaning": "to King Ikshvaku, on his part",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "alambuSaayaam",
          "iast": "alambuṣāyām",
          "devanagari": "अलम्बुषायां",
          "meaning": "throguh queen Alambusa",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "parama dhaarmikaH",
          "iast": "parama dhārmikaḥ",
          "devanagari": "परम धार्मिकः",
          "meaning": "most, righteous one [is born]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vishaala iti vishrutaH",
          "iast": "viśāla iti viśrutaḥ",
          "devanagari": "विशाल इति विश्रुतः",
          "meaning": "Vishaala, as, renowned",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "putraH utpannaH",
          "iast": "putraḥ utpannaḥ",
          "devanagari": "पुत्रः उत्पन्नः",
          "meaning": "a son, is born",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
