          "devanagari": "काकुत्स्थ इति विश्रुतः",
          "meaning": "Kakutstha, thus, highly reputed one.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.47.17",
      "label": "1.47.17",
      "numbers": [
        17
      ],
      "devanagari": "तस्य पुत्रो महातेजाः संप्रत्येष पुरीमिमाम् |\nआवसत्परमप्रख्यः सुमतिर्नाम दुर्जयः",
      "iast": "tasya putro mahātejāḥ samprati eṣa purīm imām |\nāvasat parama prakhyaḥ sumatiḥ nāma durjayaḥ",
      "translation": "\"Presently that Kakutstha's son named Sumati, who is a great-resplendent one, an unconquerable one, and a highly celebrated one is dwelling in this city.",
      "notes": [
        "These two Ikshvaku and Kakutstha are of Vishaala dynasty. They are not to be confounded with the grandparents of Rama."
